# lib/ is Composer's output, committed on purpose: there is no build step and no
# Composer on the web server, so the deploy zip is the working tree. See the
# "Bundled libraries" section of the README.
#
# Marking it vendored and generated tells GitHub to leave it out of the
# repository's language statistics, collapse it by default in pull requests, and
# skip it in blame — so 689 files nobody here wrote stop drowning the ~1,500
# lines that were.
#
# Deliberately NOT marked `-diff`: that would hide the contents of a dependency
# bump, which is the one time somebody genuinely needs to read these files.
lib/** linguist-vendored
lib/** linguist-generated
